{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/794774-what-if-a-sin-eater-and-their-geist-wanted-to-have-children","id":794774,"title":"What If A Sin-Eater And Their Geist Wanted To Have Children?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-29T05:33:24-08:00","id":794774,"title":"What If A Sin-Eater And Their Geist Wanted To Have Children?","content":"Yeah, weird question, I know. A lot of Geister are just plain monstrous in appearance and don't wrap their heads around human feelings all that well (and explaining why mommy/daddy is a ghost is a whole different can of worms), but let's make an exception for the sake of story. My first guess is that they would have to travel to a Dead Dominion with a Kerberos who is like a fertility deity of some sort, and earn its favor through a grueling but ultimately fulfilling quest. But what would such a quest entail? Maxing out Synergy and keeping it there for a time while the Kerberos sends agents to test the would-be parents?<br /> <br /> I mean, it can't be as simple as buying a Ceremony that lets the Geist ride a fresh corpse (which is disrespectful to the deceased in question, to say the least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-29-2015, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T09:52:08-08:00","id":794903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/794774-what-if-a-sin-eater-and-their-geist-wanted-to-have-children#post794774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it can't be as simple as buying a Ceremony that lets the Geist ride a fresh corpse (which is disrespectful to the deceased in question, to say the least).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wings of the Moth, I think is the one you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Also due to the duration of the Ceremony, the Sin-Eater needs to be female, unless you also have some sort of acceleration for the baby's growth (with ST permission, you might be able to use a Spring Changeling's &quot;Yesterday's Birth&quot; to accelerate the pregnancy, if the Sin-Eater is a male).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:06:41-08:00","id":794914,"title":"","content":"Is the Geist even really a separate entity, once Bound, though? Makes it rather hard for them to animate an independent vessel.<br /> <br /> Also, I love how weird and WTF this question is, and yet how I can still totally see it come up in a Geist game and not look too wonky.<br /> <hr /><br /> I know there are Underworld rivers that confer supernatural fertility. And that everything is &quot;solid&quot; (considered the same ephemera) in the Underworld, thus solving the material/immaterial problem. Main issue is whether a Geist can be truly apart from their Sin-Eater. Even things like Phantasmal Marionette have the Sin-Eater possess their Geist.<br /> <br /> Gives whole new context to &quot;go screw yourself&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-29-2015, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:35:03-08:00","id":794929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/794774-what-if-a-sin-eater-and-their-geist-wanted-to-have-children?p=794914#post794914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Geist even really a separate entity, once Bound, though? Makes it rather hard for them to animate an independent vessel.<br /> <br /> Also, I love how weird and WTF this question is, and yet how I can still totally see it come up in a Geist game and not look too wonky.<br /> <hr /><br /> I know there are Underworld rivers that confer supernatural fertility. And that everything is &quot;solid&quot; (considered the same ephemera) in the Underworld, thus solving the material/immaterial problem. Main issue is whether a Geist can be truly apart from their Sin-Eater. Even things like Phantasmal Marionette have the Sin-Eater possess their Geist.<br /> <br /> Gives whole new context to &quot;go screw yourself&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if Technolyze: Edit &amp; I has a girl have sex with her own central nervous system, I can <i>damn well</i> have kids with the voice in my head!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:58:36-08:00","id":794950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/794774-what-if-a-sin-eater-and-their-geist-wanted-to-have-children?p=794929#post794929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, if Technolyze: Edit &amp; I has a girl have sex with her own central nervous system, I can <i>damn well</i> have kids with the voice in my head!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Timmy, I've told you before, put your hand back on when company is over.&quot;<br /> <br /> But if you even become separated, who has custody?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T12:38:15-08:00","id":795019,"title":"","content":"I feel weird answering this but have you checked out &quot;Goblin Midwife&quot; contract from <i>Changeling the Lost</i>, specifically <i>Goblin Markets, </i>page 25. I bet this would help if you could get the Sin-eater and Geist to perform the procreative act, possibly with the Wings of the Moth.<br /> <br /> If not that, then appealing to a spirit with Influence: Pregnancy 4 or equivalent for help could get the job done. I ran a game in Tempe AZ with Kokopelli plotting against two lovers who both had First Changes to become Foresaken (Player Character of Course), and that spirit had that influence.<br /> <br /> As a side note: That sounds like an extremely unhealthy relationship to have with a geist seeing as by definition it has made itself an abstracted aspect of death alienated from humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgr